  {
   "tipo": "explicacion",
   "titulo": {
    "@es": "Some y any",
    "@en": "Some and any"
   },
   "texto": [
    {
     "@es": "Con plurales, **some** va en afirmaciones: **There are some chairs** (hay algunas sillas).",
     "@en": "With plurals, **some** goes in statements: **There are some chairs** (there are some chairs)."
    },
    {
     "@es": "**Any** suele ir en negaciones y preguntas neutras: **There aren't any chairs**, **Are there any chairs?** En ofrecimientos y peticiones es normal **some**.",
     "@en": "**Any** usually goes in negations and neutral questions: **There aren't any chairs**, **Are there any chairs?** In offers and requests is normal **some**."
    },
    {
     "@es": "Para preguntar la cantidad: **How many rooms are there?** (¿cuántas habitaciones hay?).",
     "@en": "To ask the amount: **How many rooms are there?** (how many rooms are there?)."
    }
   ]
